{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKAKtUBY5hYeww486mN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Don't approve the two months as requested\n\nThe data shows a demand problem. Personalisation won't fix that.\n\n- **91% never opened it.** Personalisation only helps people who use the feature, so it does nothing for the 91%. Either users didn't find it or they didn't want it.\n- **Roughly 87% of those who tried it didn't come back.** 1.2% of 9% means only about 1 in 8 triers returned in week two.\n- **There's no business effect.** Users had the same basket value as matched non-users, even though they self-selected and were probably more engaged. That points to no real value.\n- **\"We're close\" isn't backed by evidence.** Ask the team which metric would move, by how much, and why they believe it. The five months already spent shouldn't influence the decision.\n\n## What I'd do instead\n\n1. **Pause feature building.** Give a small slice of the team 2–3 weeks to answer two questions:\n   - **Can people find it?** If it was buried, test more prominent placement cheaply (a home-screen card, a post-checkout prompt) and see whether trial rates rise.\n   - **Why did the 1.2% stay and the rest leave?** Interview both groups. If the few repeat users share a clear need, such as families planning a week of meals, there may be a narrower product worth building.\n2. **Agree on kill criteria in advance.** For example: at least 25% of triers return in week two and there's a measurable lift in order frequency or basket value. If the test misses, shelve the feature and move the team to something else.\n3. **Check the metric.** Basket value may be the wrong measure. Order frequency or retention could matter more for a meal planner, so look at those before ruling it out completely.\n\nOnly fund personalisation if the cheap tests show real demand. Right now they'd be refining a feature very few people are using."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3583,"cache_read_input_tokens":4609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3583},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31e2a4f5-4f7c-47e8-b035-62c0236bf636","uuid":"72a32afd-86f6-4cf0-9f54-89a78991b43a","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:24:03.917Z","request_id":"req_011CftKAKg4cJ3C8NyvzH6bR"}
